From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:30:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: AVS2: do not offer the 32x32 tiled capture format

The AVS2 mode of the H.265 engine does not write NV12_32L32. An 8-bit
832x480 stream decoded into it gave no correct picture (the same stream
into NV12 matches the reference), and a 416x240 stream never raised the
interrupt ("frame processing timed out"). The vendor library never asks
the engine for it: Avs2MallocFbmBuffer() turns every requested output
format other than NV21 and NV12 into YV12.

GStreamer prefers the tiled format when the driver offers it, so 8-bit
AVS2 failed there while FFmpeg, which takes the NV12 default, worked.
Leave NV12_32L32 out of the capture formats of AVS2.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -186,6 +186,19 @@
 
 #define CEDRUS_FORMATS_COUNT	ARRAY_SIZE(cedrus_formats)
 
+/*
+ * The AVS2 mode of the H.265 engine does not write the 32x32 tiled format:
+ * the pictures come out wrong, or the engine never raises its interrupt.
+ * The vendor library does not use it for AVS2 either, it only decodes AVS2
+ * into YV12, NV21 or NV12.
+ */
+static bool cedrus_format_unsupported(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx,
+				      const struct cedrus_format *fmt)
+{
+	return fmt->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_32L32 &&
+	       ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS2_FRAME;
+}
+
 static struct cedrus_format *cedrus_find_format(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx,
 						u32 pixelformat, u32 directions)
 {
@@ -207,6 +220,9 @@
 		    fmt->src_format != ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat)
 			continue;
 
+		if (cedrus_format_unsupported(ctx, fmt))
+			continue;
+
 		if (fmt->pixelformat == pixelformat)
 			break;
 
@@ -396,6 +412,9 @@
 		    fmt->src_format != ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat)
 			continue;
 
+		if (cedrus_format_unsupported(ctx, fmt))
+			continue;
+
 		if (index == f->index)
 			break;
 
